id: pm-x8jdt8
title: "GH-1351: leaf get advertises empty children as omitted"
description: A full get/read/show of a leaf item marks children omitted despite zero children; the suggested follow-up returns an empty rollup. Correct materiality in the SDK without hiding populated children or notes.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-29T14:54:09.941Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-29T16:17:26.235Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-29T16:17:25.502Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-29T16:17:25.502Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "Real isolated tracker proves a parent with one child and a leaf with zero children across get, show, and read; full leaf reads have no empty children omission; populated omitted children retain recovery guidance; previously repaired notes behavior remains correct"
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: medium
confidence: 90
resolution: "SDK get output materiality now uses the computed child rollup and retains conservative container guidance before a rollup is requested, without adding ordinary Task corpus scans."
expected_result: "Full leaf get, show, and read do not advertise empty children; parent reads with material children retain restoration guidance, and explicitly requested empty rollups remain visible."
actual_result: "Linked SDK and CLI transport tests passed, full repository 9,433 passing with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, and isolated packed CLI and Bun 1.3.5 public SDK acceptance proved zero-child full leaf receipt and populated parent count."
